33,2,1,talk,Servas,,"My research suggests a sobering pattern: tools requiring broad daily participation tend to fail, while specialized tools for a single trade endure. We must be careful not to fund a project that is too ambitious in its scope.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I found that the capital line is frozen, but there is still room in the recurring software allowance. Also, fixed-fee work has stayed stable, while per-head licenses tend to increase in cost.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,1,talk,Sakura,,"Oh boy, we have a problem! The in-house developers are busy until the third quarter, and the network coverage at customer plants is really spotty—some places lose signal for whole afternoons!","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"My findings confirm significant waste; we are losing nearly an hour daily to copying existing records, and misrouted deliveries are happening because different units hold conflicting addresses for the same firms.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"I discovered that the coordination group is understaffed due to a hiring freeze, and our clerks are wasting time requesting the same certificates from vendors multiple times. The administrative burden is quite high.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,Servas,,It is clear that we are facing a conflict between significant operational waste and a lack of available resources. We must find a solution that is sustainable and does not overstretch our staff.,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"I agree. Since the capital budget is frozen, we should probably avoid anything that requires a large upfront investment and instead look for something that fits within the software allowance.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Sakura,,"Wait, if the developers are busy and the network is bad, we can't do anything that needs a lot of coding right now or relies on the internet at plants! That's a huge deal!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Sakura, that is a critical point. If we cannot rely on connectivity or immediate developer support, we must prioritize a solution that addresses the data duplication and delivery errors without requiring a complex, real-time infrastructure.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"Exactly. We also cannot ignore the staffing shortage. Any proposal that adds more manual coordination or administrative overhead to an already exhausted team will likely fail, regardless of its technical merit.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,3,talk,Servas,,"We must seek a balance. We need a tool that solves these tangible inefficiencies—like the record copying and vendor queries—but remains narrow enough in scope to survive without constant, broad-scale maintenance.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I think we should be very careful about the licensing costs too. If we pick something that scales per person, the cost might jump unexpectedly next year.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Sakura,,I'm with Daisuke! We need something that won't break the bank later and doesn't need a super-genius coder to fix it every time it crashes!,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"If we prioritize the reduction of daily record-copying and the resolution of conflicting supplier addresses, we can target the most significant operational losses while keeping the project scope manageable.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"I agree with Ryuji. We should look for a proposal that streamlines data management to reduce the burden on our clerks and coordination group, provided it doesn't require extensive new staffing.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,4,talk,Servas,,"It seems we have reached a consensus on the criteria. We need a focused solution that reduces administrative waste without requiring heavy capital, constant connectivity, or excessive manpower. I am ready to see the candidates.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,I'm ready too. I hope there's something that fits all these constraints.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Sakura,,I'm ready! Let's see if any of these ideas are actually doable!,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,I am also ready. Let us evaluate the candidates against the operational realities we have uncovered.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Asuka,,I am ready. Let us see which proposal best aligns with our resource constraints and operational needs.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
